{"content":"Perfect! Now I have all the information. Let me compile the answer:\n\nq29.\n\n**Interceptor path:** `web/src/connect.ts` (lines 156-178, function `authInterceptor`)\n\n**Token kinds managed:** \n1. **Access Token V2** (short-lived JWT, ~15 minutes) — managed by `authInterceptor` which calls `getRequestToken()` \n2. **Refresh Token** (long-lived, stored in HTTP-only cookie) — used for token refresh via `refreshAccessToken()` / `doRefreshAccessToken()`\n3. **Personal Access Token (PAT)** (long-lived for programmatic access) — mentioned in backend but not used by the frontend interceptor\n\n**Backend validation package:** `server/auth` (path: `server/auth/authenticator.go`)\n\nThe backend package exports `Authenticator` which:\n- Validates Access Token V2 via `AuthenticateByAccessTokenV2()` \n- Validates Refresh Tokens via `AuthenticateByRefreshToken()`\n- Validates PATs via `AuthenticateByPAT()`\n- Orchestrates all three via the `Authenticate()` method called by `AuthInterceptor` in `server/router/api/v1/connect_interceptors.go` (lines 208-231)","iteration":12,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
